Atorvastatin calcium is the calcium salt form of atorvastatin, a pharmaceutical compound used as an active ingredient in medicines that lower cholesterol. Atorvastatin belongs to the statin class and works by inhibiting an enzyme involved in cholesterol production. Approved atorvastatin medicines are prescribed for appropriate patients to manage elevated cholesterol and reduce cardiovascular risk as part of a broader treatment plan.
